          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "calx \"heel\" is a native Latin noun with no settled origin; Lewis & Short keeps it apart from calx \"lime\". English recalcitrant comes from it, through recalcitrō \"to kick back\"."
            }
          ]
        },
